            "review_title": "Review at Les Artisans de l'Indochine",
            "review_text": "Hilts\nDa Nang, Vietnam533 contributions\n4\nIf you’re craving some charcuterie and French cheese, you have to go here\nJan 2026 • Friends\nService:\n- Everyone I interacted with was extremely welcoming, friendly, knowledgeable and helpful.\n- A special thank you to Justin, who explained everything about the different cheeses and meats he offers and Vi who was very attentive and provided great customer service.\n- I also really appreciated Justin letting me taste the different cheeses and meats as this helped me to choose what I wanted.\n- Rating: 5/5\n\nAtmosphere:\n- They have both indoor and outdoor seating.\n- For the best views I recommend the balcony, but you also have lovely views from the ground floor terrace. The views of the paddy fields are stunning, especially during sunset.\n- Seating: High-back deck chairs.\n- During my visit there was no music, but one of the neibours was having a party / karaoke, which created a great atmosphere.\n- Crowd: Mainly Expats\n- Rating: 5/5\n\nMy Order:\n- 1 x Charcuterie (Meat) platter.\n- Overall Rating: 5/5\n- 1 x Fromage (Cheese) platter.\n- I also had some pickles and a baguette.\n- I tried numerous white and red wine, which during happy hour only cost 65K per glass.\n- 6 x Glasses of wine (Red & White)\n- 2 x Huda\n- 1 x Sparkling bottle of water (330ml): 25K\n- Everything I tasted was incredible.\n- Total price: 927,300 VND\n- Rating: 5/5\n\nOverall Rating: 5/5\n\nAdditional Information:\n- Happy Hour: 13:00 to 16:00.\n- A selection of wines are only 65K per glass.\n\nEverything I tasted was incredible and reminded me of the time I lived in Paris.\n\nIt’s great that Justin works with local farmers to produce such amazing food!\n\nA Big thank you to Justin, his wife and his team for such an incredible experience.\n\nIf you love French food and you’re in Hoi An or Da Nang, I highly recommend you visit Les Artisans de l’Indochine.\n\nPlease support this Amazing business! 🙏\n\nSee you soon Justin and Team.\n\nEnjoy 🍷 🧀 🥖 🥩\nRead more\nWritten September 24, 2026",
