            "review_text": "Jack N\nChicago, Illinois16 contributions\n0\nA Deeply Memorable Riverside Wine & Charcuterie Experience in Da Nang\nMar 2026 • Solo\nTucked along the banks of the Han River, Les Artisans de l’Indochine offers one of the most memorable food experiences I’ve had in Da Nang. This small, welcoming bistro specializes in importing outstanding wines, cheeses, sausages, salamis, and cured meats from around the world, and the care that goes into selecting these flavors is immediately clear.\n\nThe charcuterie selection is exceptional. The cheeses and cured meats deliver layers of flavor—sweet, spicy, earthy, and deeply savory. Each bite carries real complexity, with peppery notes and rich umami that linger pleasantly. Paired with sliced, toasted baguette and a glass of house red wine, the combination creates a wonderful balance of textures and flavors that makes you want to slow down and savor every bite.\n\nThe setting makes the experience even more special. From the terrace you can relax and enjoy the riverside atmosphere of the Han River. At night, the nearby Dragon Bridge lights up with colorful displays, and you can watch boats moving along the water while visitors stroll up and down the promenade. Looking across the river toward downtown Da Nang, the scene feels vibrant but unhurried—perfect for a long, relaxed evening.\n\nThe owner, Jeff, adds a personal touch to the experience. He clearly has a deep understanding of flavors and is happy to guide guests through the menu. My recommendation: ask him what he suggests and be open to trying something new. Whether you lean adventurous or prefer to stay within your comfort zone, there will be something here that surprises and delights you.\n\nOn my visit, I chose a charcuterie board paired with a house red and several soft cheeses—smoky, spicy, and wonderfully flavorful. The cured meats and cheeses together created a rich, satisfying bite on toasted baguette that made the entire experience feel indulgent in the best possible way.\n\nPlaces like this are rare—intimate, thoughtful, and clearly built with passion. Les Artisans de l’Indochine is the kind of place you hope to return to again and again, hoping to rediscover even a small piece of the joy you experienced the first time.\n\nHighly recommended for anyone in Da Nang who appreciates great wine, fine cheeses, and a beautiful riverside setting.\nRead more\nWritten March 15, 2026",
